let refinementWorker='founder';
HELP_TOPICS.push({id:'refinements',title:'Commissions, routines and practical projects',tags:'commissions income routine evening work task objective signature memory resonance',view:'commissions',sections:[
 ['External commissions','Choose a worker and one payment before accepting. Each order takes two assigned work phases; payment is fixed at acceptance. One household order can be active. Each client offers another order the day after delivery. Crowns and materials go into shared stores. A client lesson awards that worker one advancement point once. Pausing keeps progress; cancelling returns the committed materials and gives no payment.'],
 ['Work routines','In Work arrangements, choose an existing individual project or a provision target. Choose Rest or an existing paid follow-up project as the stopping action. With evening rest enabled, that worker rests on the evening Advance and resumes unfinished work the next morning. Changing their assignment pauses the routine. Travellers need an explicit resume at home. Preview Advance lists assignment changes; routines never advance time or purchase work.'],
 ['Practical companion projects','Iona can add route plans after completing her atlas. Zahra can develop fitting gauges after a completed patrol. Sylva can create specimen beds after a nursery discovery or observation patrol. Each improvement takes its owner three assigned phases, 10 crowns and its listed materials. The project card states the exact field effect. Cancelling unfinished work returns the original costs.'],
 ['Objective patrols and practical magic','Choose a delivery, rescue, observation or crossing repair after Chapter 7. Each has an initial site obstacle and one enemy encounter. Ordinary site work takes three phases, or two with Fieldcraft rank 1. A prepared spell can change the site condition in one phase; any conscious party member can then finish the practical work in one phase. Listed casting materials are reserved on selection and refunded if you withdraw before casting completes. Completed casts are not refunded.'],
 ['Complete the objective','Completing two task steps finishes an objective without enemy loot; the announced retaliation still applies. Observation is safe with Fieldcraft rank 1 or a prepared Wisp scout. On a crossing-repair patrol with two conscious members, protection and control actions allow one repair step. Fighting or negotiating can also complete the job. Successful return pays the objective reward; retreat does not. Each objective awards one advancement point per participant once.'],
 ['Personal signature growth','Keep the completed signature item equipped in the household equipment set for commissions and practical projects, or the expedition equipment set for patrols. Two different enemy types or work accomplishments unlock rank one; four unlock rank two. The scholar and each named companion also have a personal refinement with its exact numerical effect shown in the Armoury. Only one refinement is active.'],
 ['Follow-up conversations','Completed companion work, actual protection, successful objective patrols and shared survey discoveries create a limited set of optional invitations. They appear in the existing activity feed, companion Relationships and the journal. Planning another outing records a suggested party for review; it does not dispatch anyone. Invitations do not expire or award repeatable relationship points.'] ]});
